<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">West Sussex</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">West Sussex is a county in south-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">English Channel</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chichester">Chichester</a> as its county town. It became a separate administrative county in 1889, and together with East Sussex it covers the land of the old kingdom of the South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a>. Its landscape includes the South Downs and a coastal plain with resort towns.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/west-sussex.jpg" alt="West Sussex" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AndyScott · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:South_Downs_Way_-_Landale_brothers_view_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
